  "system": {
    "slug": "fenris-mech",
    "details": {
      "level": {
        "value": 1
      },
      "publicNotes": "<p>FENRIS Mechs are quadruped security constructs built by Hahne-Kedar, wearing the same white plating and red running lights as the company's other models. Most people call them attack dogs, and they behave like them: they accelerate to a gallop, leap with the rear legs, bring a target down with the front ones, and taser whatever they have pinned. They are less common than the LOKI and are usually deployed alongside them &mdash; on Alliance colonies, aboard merchant freighters, and by the Blue Suns.</p><p>Their sensor package is built for detection work, reading weapons and chemical traces the way a sniffer dog would.</p><p><strong>Construct Immunities:</strong> Immune to disease, mental effects, poison, sleep, and paralysis.</p><p><strong>No Shields:</strong> A FENRIS carries no kinetic barrier. Its protection is a Light Combat Frame &mdash; 20 Armor Points over the chassis &mdash; and its speed.</p><p><strong>Weakness 3 to electricity:</strong> Disruptor rounds cook the chassis. Incendiary rounds are handled by the armour it wears, which they burn through at the usual accelerated rate.</p><p><strong>Pack Deployment:</strong> FENRIS mechs swarm. A crate releases four or more at once, and the danger is the pack reaching a firing line together rather than any one mech's attack.</p>",
      "privateNotes": "<p>The post-mortem explosion is the trap. A FENRIS that hits 0 HP does not die &mdash; it drops where it stands, and anything that damages the wreck sets it off. Players who reflexively put an extra round into a downed enemy will find out once; after that, the deactivated chassis becomes terrain they have to route around. Tell them the mech has gone still, not that it is destroyed.</p>",
      "publication": {
        "title": "Mass Effect Compendium",
        "authors": "nscarpinatodev",
        "license": "ORC",
        "remaster": true
      },
      "languages": {
        "value": [],
        "details": ""
      },
      "blurb": "Hahne-Kedar quadruped security mech that runs down its target, tasers it prone, and detonates if the wreck is disturbed."
    },
